  <section class="hub-note" aria-label="How the tools connect">
    <p><strong>Your inputs follow you.</strong> Each page hands your plan to the next one &mdash; stack, retirement year and withdrawal land in the next tool&rsquo;s inputs rather than in a blank form. Every page also writes its state into the address bar, so a link you save or send comes back to exactly the plan you were looking at.</p>
    <p><strong>One model, stated plainly.</strong> All four run on the same projection engine against the same growth path, so they cannot disagree with each other about what a plan does. That growth path is the <a href="/the-power-law">Power Law</a> &mdash; a regression on bitcoin&rsquo;s entire price history, used as a central-tendency assumption and not as a forecast. Its implied growth rate declines with time, which is why the honest version of every answer here is checked across a whole horizon rather than asserted from a single year.</p>
  </section>

